{
  "an10.5:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 10.5 ",
  "an10.5:0.2": "1. Benefits ",
  "an10.5:0.3": "Vital Conditions (3rd) ",
  "an10.5:1.1": "There Venerable Ānanda addressed the mendicants … ",
  "an10.5:1.2": "“Reverends, an unethical person, who lacks ethics, has destroyed a vital condition for having no regrets. ",
  "an10.5:1.3": "When there are regrets, one who has regrets has destroyed a vital condition for joy. ",
  "an10.5:1.4": "When there is no joy, one who lacks joy has destroyed a vital condition for rapture. ",
  "an10.5:1.5": "When there is no rapture, one who lacks rapture has destroyed a vital condition for tranquility. ",
  "an10.5:1.6": "When there is no tranquility, one who lacks tranquility has destroyed a vital condition for bliss. ",
  "an10.5:1.7": "When there is no bliss, one who lacks bliss has destroyed a vital condition for right immersion. ",
  "an10.5:1.8": "When there is no right immersion, one who lacks right immersion has destroyed a vital condition for true knowledge and vision. ",
  "an10.5:1.9": "When there is no true knowledge and vision, one who lacks true knowledge and vision has destroyed a vital condition for disillusionment and dispassion. ",
  "an10.5:1.10": "When there is no disillusionment and dispassion, one who lacks disillusionment and dispassion has destroyed a vital condition for knowledge and vision of freedom. ",
  "an10.5:1.11": "Suppose there was a tree that lacked branches and foliage. Its shoots, bark, softwood, and heartwood would not grow to fullness. 